# CSS

**Status:** current. `:deep` piercing is **planned** (not shipped).

`@css { … }` is raw CSS (no interpolations). File-level and component-level
blocks concatenate in source order at that scope. Component CSS is a preamble
item like `@let`.

Lowering stamps `data-rocci-css` and wraps rules in CSS `@scope`. Authors keep
writing `class="card"`. Document chrome belongs on `body` or `:scope`, not
`html { … }`. Patch fragments should not carry a sibling `<style>`.

**Example:** [Styling](/examples/styling/).

**Limits:** no `:deep` yet.

**Related:** [Markup](/docs/templates/markup/).
